    thinking: "**Defining Imaging Suite Needs**\n\nI\'m now identifying the key features needed for a comprehensive medical imaging clinic management system. Thinking about the user\'s need to manage an imaging clinic, I am currently exploring all the relevant features, with an eye toward a complete \"Radiology & Medical Imaging Suite\". The focus is on functionality to meet the needs of such clinics.\n\n\n**Detailing Appointment Scheduling**\n\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the appointment scheduling component. My thoughts now encompass detailed modality and protocol selection, contrast agent management, and the crucial pre-study requirements checklist. The aim is to create a robust and intuitive system for appointment creation, including a visual calendar to improve the imaging clinic\'s workflow.\n\n\n**Refining Study Workflow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on study workflow within the system, specifically the status flow: Scheduled, Confirmed, Waiting Room, In Acquisition/Study, Study Completed, In Interpretation, Report Signed, and Delivered. Quick filters are essential by modality, status, date, doctor, and priority.\n\n\n**Developing Imaging Viewer Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into imaging viewer enhancements, and have finalized plans for calculation tools like Mean HU / Area calculations, plus annotation capabilities. Color maps and split-screen modes are also key, including cinematic DICOM HUD overlays for rich contextual data. I am also working on a radiologist reporting panel and am thinking on AI assistance for report generation, plus audio dictation and digital signatures.\n\n\n**Expanding Patient Records**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the patient\'s clinical history and longitudinal record features. I\'m focusing on the comprehensive directory and detailed profiles. Key elements include personal data, a robust safety and risk profile with allergy and implant alerts, plus a chronological study timeline. The design will include clinical evolution, referring physician notes, and secure document attachments. Also, I am thinking of including export functionality and a shareable report viewer link.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 975100747
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
