  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m deep-diving into the user\'s needs, specifically the email and SMS notification system. My focus is on the recall system for appointments. I\'m carefully analyzing the configuration of lead times and channels, wanting to ensure flexibility and elegance. I want to build a solution that\'s not only comprehensive but also seamless.\n\n\n**Defining Notification Rules**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the notification rules. I\'m focusing on those default, but configurable, lead times\342\200\22448 hours, 24 hours, etc. I\'ve got the active channels in mind: Email, SMS, and WhatsApp. Automated templates are also being designed, based on the study type, and will include placeholders for personalization like patient names, appointment times, etc.\n\nI\'m now designing the notification center and logs. I\'m focusing on visualizing the history of sent, pending, and scheduled notifications. Key details will be a timestamp, delivery status, channel, recipient, and message summary. I\'m also including a \"Send Manual Reminder / Resend\" button.\n\n\n**Designing Notification Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating notification previews, interactive simulators for both email (responsive HTML) and SMS. I\'m focusing on user experience, and plan to save configurations in `localStorage` with defaults. I\'m also planning endpoints on `server.ts`: `/api/notifications/send` and `/api/notifications/preview` for generating and formatting via IA or medical templates. I want users to have a great experience.\n\nI\'m now designing a secure and user-friendly web portal for patients. It will be accessible via a dedicated link, with independent login. I\'m prioritizing secure login with unique credentials. It will utilize DNI/ID plus a unique access code or birthdate. I\'m also including demo patient selectors for instant, interactive testing.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 314300870
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
